Spec: Human review and operation recovery

Purpose:
  Bind explicit decisions to fully rendered snapshots and recover uncertain operations without replay.

Owns:
  ./ReviewWorkflow.cs

Must:
  Require a rendered snapshot and fresh action-specific confirmation before any decision.
  Persist the operation receipt before calling the Broker; failed persistence sends no decision.
  Block new decisions while a prepared receipt remains unresolved and never automatically resend or replace its operation UUID.
  Recover by querying and matching the original operation result; acknowledgement failure retains recovery state.
  Permit explicit abandonment only after an unknown-operation query and a separate warning confirmation, without changing Broker state.
  Distinguish historical results from current approval and discard selection after every decision attempt.
  Use bounded commands and fixed error codes without raw exceptions.
  Inspect pending permission requests read-only and clear declaration selection during request navigation; provide no grant approval action.
